  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "City page lists APNs 841-14-007, -008 and -009, which are no longer in the county parcel layer. The county layer shows 841-14-085 at 6730 Monterey Rd, used here. City page gives 112 parking spaces in the description and 111 in its FAQ.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001415"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC CA-24-492: Monterey Family Apartments, located at 6730, 6630, 6680 Monterey Road in Gilroy on a 2.86 acre site, requested and is being recommended for a reservation of $2,661,199 in annual federal tax credits and $15,209,048 in total state tax credits and $28,570,598 of tax-exempt bond cap to finance the new construction of 94 units of housing, consisting of 93 restricted rental units, and 1 unrestricted manager's unit.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001627"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CalHFA staff report: tax credit investor changed from R4 Capital to Aegon USA Realty Advisors, LLC, and architect changed from Withee Malcolm to KTGY. SF YIMBY (November 2024) names BSB Design as architect.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003061",
        "SRC-003062"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CalHFA staff report: managing general partner PacH San Jose Holdings, LLC (owned by Pacific Housing, Inc.); administrative general partner Monterey Family Apartments, LLC, sole member ROEM West, Inc. (Stephen Emami and Robert Emami); CalHFA MIP subordinate loan $1,500,000 at 3%; construction sources total $57,512,129; appraised as-is land value $4,750,000.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003061"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SF YIMBY reports 10 extremely low-income, 10 very low-income and 73 low-income units plus a manager's unit, about 105,100 square feet across four buildings, and 112 parking spaces. City page gives a maximum height of 38 feet and building and grading permits issued June 22, 2026.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003062",
        "SRC-001415"
      ]
    }
  ],
